From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ExposureMG <exposuremg@protonmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 01:32:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/14] pan/kmod: support Windows through libdrm-win

On Windows, a panthor-compatible kernel driver (panfrost-win's panwin.sys)
is reached through libdrm-win, a libdrm-compatible DLL whose DRM fds are
emulated and can't be used with the CRT open()/close()/dup()/mmap().

- Add pan_kmod_fd_{open,dup,close}() and use them for the DRM fd in kmod
  and panvk; they map to libdrm-win's panwin_*() on Windows.
- panthor: map BOs and the LATEST_FLUSH_ID page through panwin_mmap() on
  Windows (placed/MAP_FIXED mappings are not supported there), unmap
  through bo_munmap, use os_get_page_size() instead of getpagesize(), and
  keep mmap offsets 64-bit (off_t is 32-bit on LLP64 Windows).
- Don't build the JM (panfrost) KMD backend on Windows: it needs
  eventfd/timerfd/poll and there is no Windows JM kernel driver.

Generated-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
